# The README example leaves a timing record, so its upload step has one (#529)

`readme.yml` ran the README example as `python -m doctest README.md`.  That loads
no pytest plugin and calls no timed stage, so the run wrote no `.timings/`, and
the upload step — `if-no-files-found: error` since `c68730d47` — failed the job
on every push: run 43691481505 at `63797cf`, "No files were found with the
provided path: .timings/".

This patch runs the same example through pytest instead, under the repository's
own `addopts`, which load `sage_extensions.testing.timing_record`: the run then
copies its report log and JUnit file into `.timings/` and the upload step has
both.  The example itself is unchanged — `README.md` is collected as a text
doctest by `--doctest-glob=README.md`, and the step still asserts what it always
asserted.

It is a file rather than history because the connection that pushed this work
may not update a file under `.github/workflows/`: GitHub refuses such a ref for
lack of the App's `workflows` permission.

**Install (one command, from the repository root):**

```sh
git apply results/issue529-readme-record.patch
```

The diff is against `63797cf`, where the step is at line 33.

**What it was measured on.**  In the pinned image (`ghcr.io/dzackgarza/sage`
rootfs, Sage 11.0.beta5, pytest 9.1.1), at `63797cf` with only this patch's
change applied:

```
$ python -m pytest --doctest-glob=README.md README.md -v
time gates on: star import 0.27 s (ceiling 3 s), collection ceiling 6 s, each test call ceiling 20 s
rootdir: /repos/sage-extensions
configfile: pyproject.toml
collected 1 item
README.md::README.md PASSED                                              [100%]
------ generated xml file: /repos/sage-extensions/tests/.report/junit.xml ------
-------------- generated report log file: tests/.report/run.jsonl --------------
1 passed in 0.34s
$ ls .timings
junit-63797cf6f079-20261115T080741Z.xml
run-63797cf6f079-20261115T080741Z.jsonl
```

Both record files are the ones the upload step names; neither existed under the
`doctest` invocation, which wrote nothing.

diff --git a/.github/workflows/readme.yml b/.github/workflows/readme.yml
index 9aaf440..f563656 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/readme.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/readme.yml
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 name: README example
-# The README example is the smallest acceptance: it runs as a doctest on
-# every push, inside the shared Sage image.
+# The README example is the smallest acceptance: it runs on every push, under
+# this repository's own pytest configuration so that the run keeps its timing
+# record (CONTRIBUTING.md ENV-03), inside the shared Sage image.
 on:
   push: {}
   workflow_dispatch: {}
@@ -31,9 +32,13 @@ jobs:
           uv pip install --quiet --python "$sage_python" "sage-julia-bridge @ git+https://github.com/dzackgarza/sage-julia-bridge"
           uv pip install --quiet --python "$sage_python" --no-deps -e .
       - name: Run the README example
+        # Under the repository's own addopts, which load the timing plugin: the
+        # bare `python -m doctest README.md` this step used to run loaded no
+        # plugin and wrote no .timings/, so the upload below had nothing to
+        # upload and failed a green run.
         run: |
           sage_python="$("$SAGE_BIN" -c 'import sys; print(sys.executable)')"
-          "$sage_python" -m doctest README.md
+          "$sage_python" -m pytest --doctest-glob=README.md README.md
       # The run's own timing record (CONTRIBUTING.md ENV-03): the test run's
       # report log and JUnit file as the run's plugin copied them into
       # .timings/, and the stage records the library appended as it computed.
